/S /P
/P 155 0 R
/E (In May of 1947, multiple american newspapers reported that a giant sea-monster had recently attacked Tokyo, at least according to a U.S. military radio broadcast. This broadcast would ultimately turn out to be a hoax in the style of Orson Welles' infamous War of the World's broadcast from 1938, but did it influence the creation of Godzilla? Join cultural studies scholar Justin Mullis for an in-depth look at this forgotten episode from kaiju history as well as similar hoaxes in this follow-up to G-FEST 2024's "From Cryptids to Kaiju" and 2025s "From Saucers to Seijin.")
